ge and income. However, since the user is 62 and earning $180,000 this year, they may be eligible for a higher premium. It is recommended that the user consult with HR or a benefits expert to determine the exact premium and any other requirements for COBRA coverage.\n\nNote: The answer provides concrete advice based on the retrieved policy chunks and the user's specific situation.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.5 Dependent Care FSA\n2. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 35 days (280 hrs)\n3. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees\n4. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 7.3 Life & Disability Insurance\n5. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 6.1 Annual Wellness Stipend - Eligible Expenses", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": true}
