ions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 Section 1: Welcome to Nexarion Solutions\n4. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 3.2 Illinois Salary History Ban\n5. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 Full project contribution, deliver 90-day self-assessment, receive", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "79b75752-026e-44c3-8c48-13aeb7a308bc", "session_id": "c6c4e412-cfb5-49de-8ff1-6f70e3b1ab5c", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-24T17:12:14.193954", "query": "What is the correct 2025 Healthcare FSA rollover amount for Nexarion employees enrolled in NexCare Plus or Premier? Cite the relevant section(s).", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 7}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 6}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.5 Dependent Care FSA", "chunk_index": 8}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "(PPO+)", "chunk_index": 51}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement", "section_header": "No use until approved", "chunk_index": 14}], "final_answer": "The user should reference the Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide, Section 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees, for the correct rollover amount. As per the policy, the maximum rollover amount is $660 per year, effective January 1, 2025. This means that any remaining balance above $660 will be forfeited on March 15 of the following year.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees\n2. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.5 Dependent Care FSA\n3. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 (PPO+)\n4. Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement \u2014 No use until approved", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "a397c232-f04c-4426-abcf-28a84aa14297", "session_id": "f5e75184-4548-4a29-b096-3c3286e07dac", "user_id": "1263dbbc-b5af-42d2-af49-ba20324deffe", "timestamp": "2026-04-25T20:22:08.235132", "query": "I'm 62 and earning $180,000 this year. I want to put as much as I can into my 401(k) in 2025 \u2014 I know there's a regular limit and some kind of extra catch-up contribution for people my age, but I'm not sure exactly how much I'm allowed to contribute in total. I also want to make sure I'm not leaving any of Nexarion's matching money on the table. Based on the company's 401(k) policy, what's the most I can contribute, and how much would Nexarion match if I contribute up to the match limit?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "Includes all employer match and profit-sharing", "chunk_index": 12}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "Section 3: 401(k) Retirement Plan - Detailed Guide", "chunk_index": 11}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees", "chunk_index": 4}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 6}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "7.2 401(k) Retirement Plan", "chunk_index": 53}], "final_answer": "You are eligible to contribute a total of $34,750 to your 401(k) in 2025, which includes the standard limit of $23,500 plus an enhanced catch-up contribution of $11,250 for your age. \n\nTo maximize Nexarion's matching contributions, you should contribute at least 6% of your salary, which amounts to $10,800. This will allow you to receive a total matching contribution of $8,100 from Nexarion: a 100% match on the first 3% of your salary ($5,400) and a 50% match on the next 3% ($2,700). \n\nMake sure to set your contribution rate accordingly to ensure you receive the full match, and remember that contributions can be adjusted at any time, taking effect within 1-2 pay cycles.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 Includes all employer match and profit-sharing\n2. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 Section 3: 401(k) Retirement Plan - Detailed Guide\n3. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees\n4. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees\n5. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 7.2 401(k) Retirement Plan", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": true}
