{"entry_id": "88f19a4b-7709-42d1-b516-cf697de8a45d", "session_id": "17893c3d-512b-4c9a-91f5-90b152a24c2e", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-27T19:52:07.067270", "query": "What is the FSA rollover limit \u2014 the Employee Handbook says $610 but I've heard it might be different. Which amount is correct for 2025?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 6}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.5 Dependent Care FSA", "chunk_index": 8}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 7}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "(PPO+)", "chunk_index": 51}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "7.1 Open Enrollment Window", "chunk_index": 32}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "Includes all employer match and profit-sharing", "chunk_index": 12}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "35 days (280 hrs)", "chunk_index": 58}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "1.1 PTO Accrual & Carryover - California Override", "chunk_index": 4}], "final_answer": "The FSA rollover limit for 2025 is $660, as stated in the Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide (Section 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees). According to this policy, any remaining balance above $660 is forfeited on March 15 of the following year, with a grace period applying until then. The Employee Handbook references a $610 FSA rollover limit, but this amount has been updated to $660 per the revised IRS guidelines effective January 1, 2025. It's essential for the user to review and understand this policy to avoid any potential forfeitures of their FSA funds.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees\n2. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.5 Dependent Care FSA\n3. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 (PPO+)\n4. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 7.1 Open Enrollment Window\n5. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 Includes all employer match and profit-sharing\n6. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 35 days (280 hrs)\n7. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 1.1 PTO Accrual & Carryover - California Override", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "f254b000-ee20-41fe-92c6-cbcbea9dbcfd", "session_id": "555640d0-32db-46a3-a7c8-497bfabd2e3d", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T02:41:15.949238", "query": "What is the enrollment deadline for health insurance benefits for new employees?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "6.1 New Hire Enrollment", "chunk_index": 59}, {"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "6.2 Open Enrollment", "chunk_index": 60}, {"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "4.1 Benefits Eligibility", "chunk_index": 31}, {"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "6.3 Qualifying Life Events", "chunk_index": 61}, {"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "2.5 Supplemental Health Benefits", "chunk_index": 24}], "final_answer": "New employees must complete their benefits elections within 30 days of their hire date through the Workday HRIS self-service portal. Benefits elections apply on the first day of the month following 30 days of employment (or on day 1 if hired on the first of the month). Failure to elect within the 30-day window will result in the employee being defaulted into the lowest-cost medical plan, employee-only coverage, and basic life insurance only.\n\nTo ensure timely enrollment, new employees should complete their benefits elections as soon as possible after their hire date. If they miss the initial 30-day deadline, they may be able to make changes during open enrollment or within 30 days of a qualifying life event, subject to documentation requirements.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Benefits Manual \u2014 6.1 New Hire Enrollment\n2. Benefits Manual \u2014 6.2 Open Enrollment\n3. Handbook \u2014 4.1 Benefits Eligibility\n4. Benefits Manual \u2014 6.3 Qualifying Life Events\n5. Benefits Manual \u2014 2.5 Supplemental Health Benefits", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "689f99ff-700e-432a-aad6-0393a2271028", "session_id": "555640d0-32db-46a3-a7c8-497bfabd2e3d", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T02:43:29.599307", "query": "How many days of paid sick leave are employees entitled to per year?\n6. What is the process for requesting a leave of absence?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "5.3 Family and Medical Leave (FMLA)", "chunk_index": 47}, {"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "5.1 Paid Time Off (PTO)", "chunk_index": 42}, {"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "4.1 Benefits Eligibility", "chunk_index": 31}, {"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "5.4 Parental Leave", "chunk_index": 50}, {"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "4.5 Disability Insurance", "chunk_index": 38}], "final_answer": "The user is eligible for paid sick leave under the unified PTO system, which accrues per pay period based on years of continuous service. As a full-time employee, they are entitled to 30 days (240 hours) of paid sick leave per year. \n\nTo request a leave of absence, employees should follow the process outlined in the FMLA section of the handbook, which includes providing qualifying reasons for leave and completing necessary paperwork. Additionally, employees can use their accrued PTO to cover the time off.\n\nIt is essential to note that while the company provides short-term disability insurance, it does not provide paid sick leave. Employees should review their benefits package to understand the specifics of their coverage.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Handbook \u2014 5.3 Family and Medical Leave (FMLA)\n2. Handbook \u2014 5.1 Paid Time Off (PTO)\n3. Handbook \u2014 4.1 Benefits Eligibility\n4. Handbook \u2014 5.4 Parental Leave\n5. Handbook \u2014 4.5 Disability Insurance", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "6685d42d-fef0-4a3b-abe6-1d0ff33a2c30", "session_id": "555640d0-32db-46a3-a7c8-497bfabd2e3d", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T02:46:24.613944", "query": "What are the steps in the progressive discipline process?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "7.4 Progressive Discipline", "chunk_index": 68}, {"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "10.2 Involuntary Termination", "chunk_index": 84}, {"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "7.4 Progressive Discipline", "chunk_index": 69}, {"document_name": "Anti Harassment Policy", "section_header": "4.3 Corrective Action", "chunk_index": 21}, {"document_name": "Anti Harassment Policy", "section_header": "4.3 Corrective Action", "chunk_index": 22}], "final_answer": "The progressive discipline process at NovaBridge Solutions involves a standard sequence of Verbal Counseling, Written Warning, Final Written Warning, and Termination for performance and conduct issues. However, the severity of an incident may warrant bypassing one or more steps, up to and including immediate termination for serious violations. \n\nDisciplinary actions must be documented using the Performance Counseling Form (HR-PCF) and are maintained in the employee's personnel file for a period of three years for warnings and indefinitely for terminations.\n\nEmployees have the right to respond to any disciplinary action in writing within five business days, and corrective actions may include mandatory training, workplace modifications, formal disciplinary action including termination, removal from supervisory roles, or other measures as appropriate. \n\nAll employees are required to complete NovaBridge Solutions' Prevention of Workplace Harassment training upon hire and annually thereafter.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Handbook \u2014 7.4 Progressive Discipline\n2. Handbook \u2014 10.2 Involuntary Termination\n3. Anti Harassment Policy \u2014 4.3 Corrective Action", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "6e94d78e-a238-416e-8c6b-e01e0e41c9dd", "session_id": "555640d0-32db-46a3-a7c8-497bfabd2e3d", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T02:48:52.981125", "query": "What behaviors are considered grounds for immediate termination?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "10.2 Involuntary Termination", "chunk_index": 84}, {"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "1.2 At-Will Employment", "chunk_index": 5}, {"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "Confidential \u2014 Internal Use Only Page 6", "chunk_index": 18}, {"document_name": "Anti Harassment Policy", "section_header": "Anti-Harassment, Non-Discrimination", "chunk_index": 1}, {"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "Section 11: Acknowledgment and Agreement", "chunk_index": 90}], "final_answer": "The specific policies related to termination at NovaBridge Solutions include involuntary terminations for performance or conduct reasons, which typically follow a progressive discipline process. However, terminations for gross misconduct, such as theft, violence, falsification of records, or serious policy violations, may occur without prior notice or severance and are subject to review and approval by an HR Business Partner and the employee's department head.\n\nAdditionally, excessive unexcused absences or tardiness may result in progressive disciplinary action up to and including termination. However, this does not explicitly state what behaviors are considered grounds for immediate termination.\n\nThe anti-harassment policy also states that any substantiated violation of this policy will result in disciplinary action up to and including immediate termination, regardless of the level or tenure of the employee involved.\n\nGiven the lack of explicit language on specific behaviors leading to immediate termination, it is recommended that the user review their employment contract and consult with HR to understand the company's policies and procedures regarding termination.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Handbook \u2014 10.2 Involuntary Termination\n2. Handbook \u2014 1.2 At-Will Employment\n3. Handbook \u2014 Confidential \u2014 Internal Use Only Page 6\n4. Anti Harassment Policy \u2014 Anti-Harassment, Non-Discrimination\n5. Handbook \u2014 Section 11: Acknowledgment and Agreement\n\n---\n_Note: This response is for informational purposes only and does not constitute legal advice. Please consult with HR or a qualified professional for guidance on your specific situation._", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": false}
{"entry_id": "b969539c-5e94-4387-b2ef-5b1026633380", "session_id": "555640d0-32db-46a3-a7c8-497bfabd2e3d", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T02:53:32.546870", "query": "What is the process for updating an employee's personal information such as address or tax withholding?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "1.5 Equity Compensation", "chunk_index": 16}, {"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "6.2 Open Enrollment", "chunk_index": 60}, {"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "3.5 Plan Loans and Hardship Withdrawals", "chunk_index": 36}, {"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "2.6 Health Savings Account (HSA)", "chunk_index": 25}, {"document_name": "Anti Harassment Policy", "section_header": "2.1 Harassment", "chunk_index": 6}], "final_answer": "Update your address or tax withholding information during open enrollment, which typically occurs each November for January 1 effective dates. Review the benefits manual for specific instructions on how to make changes to your benefits elections. You may also need to provide documentation to support any changes to your personal information.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Benefits Manual \u2014 1.5 Equity Compensation\n2. Benefits Manual \u2014 6.2 Open Enrollment\n3. Benefits Manual \u2014 3.5 Plan Loans and Hardship Withdrawals\n4. Benefits Manual \u2014 2.6 Health Savings Account (HSA)\n5. Anti Harassment Policy \u2014 2.1 Harassment\n\n---\n_Note: This response is for informational purposes only and does not constitute legal advice. Please consult with HR or a qualified professional for guidance on your specific situation._", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": false}
{"entry_id": "8438dd3b-fe55-4512-a811-d76734e83d56", "session_id": "b3736096-8c82-4e3e-9c56-661562e6cd5e", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T14:18:18.509114", "query": "If an employee receives a mid-year promotion, when does their new compensation take effect?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "Promotional Increases", "chunk_index": 8}, {"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "1.4 Variable Pay Programs", "chunk_index": 11}, {"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "Retention Packages", "chunk_index": 10}, {"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "Benefits & Compensation Manual | Confidential12", "chunk_index": 46}, {"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "Referral Bonus", "chunk_index": 29}], "final_answer": "According to the Benefits Manual, promotional increases are usually effective on the first day of the next pay period following the promotion. This means that the employee's current salary will be adjusted to reflect their new title and responsibilities on the first day of the next pay period.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Benefits Manual \u2014 Promotional Increases\n2. Benefits Manual \u2014 1.4 Variable Pay Programs\n3. Benefits Manual \u2014 Retention Packages\n4. Benefits Manual \u2014 Benefits & Compensation Manual | Confidential12\n5. Handbook \u2014 Referral Bonus", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": false}
{"entry_id": "e62803a7-8369-4820-823b-67ef049d3533", "session_id": "b3736096-8c82-4e3e-9c56-661562e6cd5e", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T14:19:19.158744", "query": "If an employee receives a mid-year promotion, when does their new compensation take effect?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "Annual Performance Bonus", "chunk_index": 27}, {"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "1.4 Variable Pay Programs", "chunk_index": 11}, {"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "4.1 Benefits Eligibility", "chunk_index": 31}, {"document_name": "Handbook", "section_header": "3.3 Payroll Processing", "chunk_index": 23}, {"document_name": "Benefits Manual", "section_header": "3.2 Employee Contributions", "chunk_index": 30}], "final_answer": "When an employee receives a mid-year promotion, their new compensation typically takes effect at the beginning of the next pay period following the promotion announcement. Since employees are paid on a bi-weekly schedule, you should expect the new compensation to be reflected in your paycheck starting from the next scheduled pay date after the promotion is confirmed. If you have any specific concerns or need to confirm the exact timing, it would be advisable to discuss this with your HR department for clarification.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Handbook \u2014 Annual Performance Bonus\n2. Benefits Manual \u2014 1.4 Variable Pay Programs\n3. Handbook \u2014 4.1 Benefits Eligibility\n4. Handbook \u2014 3.3 Payroll Processing\n5. Benefits Manual \u2014 3.2 Employee Contributions", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": false}
{"entry_id": "6b7814e3-ce30-4ddb-9f58-4bb0b27af4a9", "session_id": "68912d30-a7a7-46b9-9135-a04d7da48706", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T14:23:35.660430", "query": "I'm enrolled in the NexCare Plus plan and I have $800 left in my Healthcare FSA at year end. How much of that can I roll over into next year, and where did I get that number?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 6}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 7}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "1.1 PTO Accrual & Carryover - California Override", "chunk_index": 4}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "35 days (280 hrs)", "chunk_index": 58}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "7.2 Qualifying Life Events (QLE)", "chunk_index": 33}], "final_answer": "You can roll over $660 of your remaining $800 in your Healthcare FSA into the next plan year. The remaining $140 will be forfeited after the grace period, which ends on March 15 of the following year. This information is based on the Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide, which specifies the rollover limit for the Healthcare FSA. Make sure to use the rolled-over funds before the grace period ends to avoid losing any remaining balance.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees\n2. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 1.1 PTO Accrual & Carryover - California Override\n3. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 35 days (280 hrs)\n4. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 7.2 Qualifying Life Events (QLE)", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": true}
