ccessing work-related systems.\n\nTaking these steps promptly will help mitigate any potential issues arising from this policy violation.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement \u2014 2.3 Approved AI Tools Policy\n2. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 12.1 Acceptable Use of Technology\n3. Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement \u2014 2.1 VPN Requirements\n4. Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement \u2014 3.3 Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) Policy", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "651d3e92-020e-4fcb-baef-68e6072f8a9f", "session_id": "6d5863b3-4a5a-4351-bb40-6382be2350f5", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T14:50:16.506122", "query": "I'm a New York-based employee and I've been out sick for 2 days. My manager is asking me to provide a doctor's note to use my PTO for those days. Do I have to provide one?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "2.1 New York Paid Sick Leave", "chunk_index": 13}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "2.1 New York Paid Sick Leave", "chunk_index": 14}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "8.1 Family & Medical Leave (FMLA)", "chunk_index": 65}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "3.1 Illinois Paid Leave for All Workers Act", "chunk_index": 19}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "5.1 Premium Payment During Unpaid Leave", "chunk_index": 23}], "final_answer": "You are not required to provide a doctor's note for your 2 days of sick leave, as New York law prohibits employers from requiring documentation for sick leave of fewer than 3 consecutive days. \n\nHere\u2019s what you should do:\n1. **Communicate with Your Manager**: Inform your manager that, according to New York policy, a doctor's note is not necessary for your absence since it was only 2 days.\n2. **Use Your PTO**: Proceed to use your PTO for those days as planned.\n\nIf your manager insists on a doctor's note despite this policy, you may want to escalate the issue to HR for clarification.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 2.1 New York Paid Sick Leave\n2. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 8.1 Family & Medical Leave (FMLA)\n3. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 3.1 Illinois Paid Leave for All Workers Act\n4. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 5.1 Premium Payment During Unpaid Leave\n\n---\n_Note: This response is for informational purposes only and does not constitute legal advice. Please consult with HR or a qualified professional for guidance on your specific situation._", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": false}
