on & Retaliation", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "2b67a652-88bc-4bc4-b389-9c265a7ecdb0", "session_id": "16c1a7fa-298b-45f3-a71a-b8e944d3c5d3", "user_id": "1263dbbc-b5af-42d2-af49-ba20324deffe", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T19:43:27.095775", "query": "I'm a California-based employee and I've accumulated 28 days of PTO. My annual accrual is 18 days (I'm in my 4th year). My manager told me anything over 26 days gets forfeited on January 1. Is that right?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "1.1 PTO Accrual & Carryover - California Override", "chunk_index": 5}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "NEXARION SOLUTIONS, INC.", "chunk_index": 60}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 8}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "3.3 Loan and Hardship Withdrawal Provisions", "chunk_index": 19}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "13.2 Offboarding Checklist", "chunk_index": 100}], "final_answer": "You are correct that your manager's statement about forfeiting PTO days is misleading. According to California law and the Nexarion policy, you cannot lose accrued PTO due to forfeiture. However, there is an accrual cap in place for California employees, which is set at 1.5 times your annual accrual rate. Since your annual accrual is 18 days, the cap is 27 days. \n\nAs you currently have 28 days of PTO, you will not lose any days, but you will stop accruing additional PTO until your balance falls below the cap. To manage your PTO effectively, consider planning to use some of your accrued days before reaching the cap to continue accruing more time off.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 1.1 PTO Accrual & Carryover - California Override\n2. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 NEXARION SOLUTIONS, INC.\n3. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees\n4. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 3.3 Loan and Hardship Withdrawal Provisions\n5. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 13.2 Offboarding Checklist", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": false}
{"entry_id": "a66b4644-6d58-4932-b646-4a637cb375dd", "session_id": "16c1a7fa-298b-45f3-a71a-b8e944d3c5d3", "user_id": "1263dbbc-b5af-42d2-af49-ba20324deffe", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T19:53:15.214690", "query": "I just turned 62. What is the maximum I can contribute to my 401(k) this year, including catch-up contributions?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "SECURE 2.0)", "chunk_index": 14}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "Section 3: 401(k) Retirement Plan - Detailed Guide", "chunk_index": 13}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 7}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees", "chunk_index": 5}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "3.3 Loan and Hardship Withdrawal Provisions", "chunk_index": 19}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "4.2 Voluntary Supplemental Life Insurance", "chunk_index": 23}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "2025 Benefits Guide  |  Confidential", "chunk_index": 25}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "2025 Benefits Guide  |  Confidential", "chunk_index": 24}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "4.2 Voluntary Supplemental Life Insurance", "chunk_index": 22}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "4.1 Company-Provided Coverage Summary", "chunk_index": 20}], "final_answer": "As of 2023, the maximum contribution limit for a 401(k) plan is $22,500. Since you have turned 62, you are eligible for a catch-up contribution of an additional $7,500, bringing your total maximum contribution to $30,000 for the year. \n\nTo maximize your contributions, ensure that you adjust your payroll deductions accordingly. If you haven't already, you may want to inform your HR or payroll department about your intention to make the catch-up contributions. Be mindful of any deadlines your company may have for adjusting contribution amounts, typically at the beginning of the year or during open enrollment periods.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 SECURE 2.0)\n2. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 Section 3: 401(k) Retirement Plan - Detailed Guide\n3. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees\n4. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees\n5. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 3.3 Loan and Hardship Withdrawal Provisions\n6. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 4.2 Voluntary Supplemental Life Insurance\n7. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 2025 Benefits Guide  |  Confidential\n8. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 4.1 Company-Provided Coverage Summary", "grounding_score": 0.5, "compliance_passed": false}
{"entry_id": "b4a13b13-b08d-4245-be51-ea10b3f5b02b", "session_id": "16c1a7fa-298b-45f3-a71a-b8e944d3c5d3", "user_id": "1263dbbc-b5af-42d2-af49-ba20324deffe", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T19:55:25.707524", "query": "I accidentally spilled coffee on my Nexarion-issued laptop. This is the second time I've damaged company equipment in the past year and a half. What am I financially responsible for, and what do I need to do?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "Section 14: Acknowledgment of Receipt", "chunk_index": 103}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "5.4 Drug Testing", "chunk_index": 33}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "Section 1: California (CA)", "chunk_index": 4}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "12.1 Acceptable Use of Technology", "chunk_index": 91}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "Section 11: Harassment, Discrimination & Retaliation", "chunk_index": 86}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "Section 10: Disciplinary Procedures", "chunk_index": 83}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement", "section_header": "1.2 Equipment Provided by Nexarion", "chunk_index": 5}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "11.2 Reporting Procedure", "chunk_index": 89}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "Section 10: Disciplinary Procedures", "chunk_index": 84}], "final_answer": "You have spilled coffee on your Nexarion-issued laptop for the second time, and it's important to address this promptly. According to company policy, you are responsible for keeping company equipment updated and must report any damage within 24 hours. Here are the steps you should take:\n\n1. **Report the Damage**: If you haven't done so already, report the incident to your HR Business Partner or the HR Director immediately. This is crucial for compliance with company policy.\n\n2. **Document the Incident**: Keep a detailed record of the incident, including when and how it happened. This documentation may be important for any discussions with HR.\n\n3. **Prepare for Possible Consequences**: Since this is the second incident, be aware that repeated damage may lead to disciplinary actions as outlined in the disciplinary procedures. While the policy does not explicitly state financial responsibility, it could be a factor in HR's review of your situation.\n\n4. **Follow Up**: After reporting, check in with HR to understand any potential consequences or next steps regarding the damaged equipment.\n\nBy taking these actions, you will be adhering to company policy and addressing the situation appropriately.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 Section 14: Acknowledgment of Receipt\n2. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 5.4 Drug Testing\n3. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 Section 1: California (CA)\n4. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 12.1 Acceptable Use of Technology\n5. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 Section 11: Harassment, Discrimination & Retaliation\n6. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 Section 10: Disciplinary Procedures\n7. Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement \u2014 1.2 Equipment Provided by Nexarion\n8. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 11.2 Reporting Procedure", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": true}
