ed. This documentation may be important for any discussions with HR.\n\n3. **Understand Financial Responsibility**: While the policy does not explicitly state that you are financially responsible for the damage, repeated incidents may lead to disciplinary actions or discussions about accountability. Be prepared for HR to review your situation, especially since this is the second occurrence.\n\n4. **Follow Up**: After reporting, check in with HR to understand any potential consequences or next steps regarding the damaged equipment. They will guide you on how to proceed and whether any financial responsibility will be assessed.\n\nBy taking these actions, you will be adhering to company policy and addressing the situation appropriately.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement \u2014 1.2 Equipment Provided by Nexarion\n2. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 11.2 Reporting Procedure\n3. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 Section 10: Disciplinary Procedures\n4. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 5.4 Drug Testing\n5. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 3.3 New Employee Orientation Program (NEOP)", "grounding_score": 0.5, "compliance_passed": false}
