{"entry_id": "6684434e-255d-432b-889f-d875733211bc", "session_id": "be8024c7-3af3-4483-b7f2-1c35a78770f2", "user_id": "27ee5d21-fd56-4372-8c47-d01c095f9e9f", "timestamp": "2026-04-29T00:09:29.103467", "query": "I'm enrolled in the NexCare Plus plan and I have $800 left in my Healthcare FSA at year end. How much of that can I roll over into next year, and where did I get that number?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 7}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 8}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "NEXARION SOLUTIONS, INC.", "chunk_index": 60}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "1.1 PTO Accrual & Carryover - California Override", "chunk_index": 5}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees", "chunk_index": 6}], "final_answer": "You can roll over $660 of your remaining $800 in your Healthcare FSA into the next year. The remaining $140 will be forfeited after the grace period, which ends on March 15 of the following year. This information is based on the policy stating that the maximum rollover amount is $660, and any balance above that is forfeited.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees\n2. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 1.1 PTO Accrual & Carryover - California Override\n3. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "b1e1f985-ebb1-4ac2-a99a-b6fa57dc7aa2", "session_id": "91782950-3f1e-4f01-a7f9-3276478eee09", "user_id": "27ee5d21-fd56-4372-8c47-d01c095f9e9f", "timestamp": "2026-04-29T00:12:10.187777", "query": "I accidentally spilled coffee on my Nexarion-issued laptop. This is the second time I've damaged company equipment in the past year and a half. What am I financially responsible for, and what do I need to do?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement", "section_header": "NEXARION SOLUTIONS, INC.", "chunk_index": 21}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement", "section_header": "NEXARION SOLUTIONS, INC.", "chunk_index": 20}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement", "section_header": "3.2 Security Incident Response Procedure", "chunk_index": 25}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "4.2 Conflict of Interest", "chunk_index": 29}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement", "section_header": "1.2 Equipment Provided by Nexarion", "chunk_index": 5}], "final_answer": "You are financially responsible for a $300 deductible due to this being the second occurrence of accidental damage within 24 months. Additionally, since the damage was caused by a liquid spill, you will also be responsible for 50% of the replacement cost of the laptop, up to a maximum of $600. \n\nTo proceed, you need to report the incident to IT within 24 hours. They will assess the damage and arrange for repair or replacement. Make sure to notify your manager as well, as they will be informed of the situation.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement \u2014 3.2 Security Incident Response Procedure\n2. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 4.2 Conflict of Interest\n3. Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement \u2014 1.2 Equipment Provided by Nexarion", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "902896e6-a3c2-4ea8-899b-c5790773118a", "session_id": "3d6739eb-d93f-446a-9003-83029a6ee487", "user_id": "27ee5d21-fd56-4372-8c47-d01c095f9e9f", "timestamp": "2026-04-29T00:18:37.582510", "query": "I accidentally spilled coffee on my Nexarion-issued laptop. This is the second time I've damaged company equipment in the past year and a half. What am I financially responsible for, and what do I need to do?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "Section 14: Acknowledgment of Receipt", "chunk_index": 103}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "2.2 Equal Opportunity Employment", "chunk_index": 12}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "5.4 Drug Testing", "chunk_index": 33}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement", "section_header": "NEXARION SOLUTIONS, INC.", "chunk_index": 21}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement", "section_header": "3.2 Security Incident Response Procedure", "chunk_index": 25}], "final_answer": "You are financially responsible for the negligent damage caused by spilling coffee on your Nexarion-issued laptop. This means you will need to pay 50% of the replacement cost, up to a maximum of $600. Additionally, since this is the second incident within 24 months, you will also need to pay a $300 deductible if IT classifies it as accidental damage instead.\n\nHere are the steps you should take:\n1. Report the incident to IT within 24 hours by submitting a ticket. They will assess the damage and determine whether it falls under accidental or negligent damage.\n2. Be aware that HR will be notified of this incident due to the second occurrence.\n3. Prepare to cover the financial responsibility based on IT's assessment, either the $300 deductible or 50% of the replacement cost, whichever applies.\n\nMake sure to act quickly to ensure compliance with the reporting requirement.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 Section 14: Acknowledgment of Receipt\n2. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 2.2 Equal Opportunity Employment\n3. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 5.4 Drug Testing\n4. Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement \u2014 3.2 Security Incident Response Procedure", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": true}
