on on enrollment deadlines or notice requirements for adding new pets to your coverage. I recommend checking with HR or Nexarion's customer service for more information on this topic.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 Section 14: Acknowledgment of Receipt\n2. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 5.4 Drug Testing\n3. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 4.2 Voluntary Supplemental Life Insurance\n4. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 7.1 Health, Dental & Vision Insurance", "grounding_score": 0.5, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "f65861d9-cd3d-4d96-b139-ed9add6af599", "session_id": "666fce05-a3e1-4119-9fa5-36c77e5b3820", "user_id": "d976e6a6-dcee-4072-859d-0c36b07e89c8", "timestamp": "2026-04-29T02:11:25.876704", "query": "I'm enrolled in the NexCare Plus plan and I have $800 left in my Healthcare FSA at year end. How much of that can I roll over into next year, and where did I get that number?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 7}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 8}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "7.1 Health, Dental & Vision Insurance", "chunk_index": 53}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.5 Dependent Care FSA", "chunk_index": 9}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees", "chunk_index": 5}], "final_answer": "The user should roll over their remaining $800 in Healthcare FSA funds into the next year. However, due to the use-it-or-lose-it policy with a $610 rollover allowance per IRS rules, the user can only roll over up to $660. The user will forfeit the excess amount of $190.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees\n2. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 7.1 Health, Dental & Vision Insurance\n3. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.5 Dependent Care FSA\n4. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "a7982136-4cd2-44a4-ab6d-17711bb412ff", "session_id": "666fce05-a3e1-4119-9fa5-36c77e5b3820", "user_id": "d976e6a6-dcee-4072-859d-0c36b07e89c8", "timestamp": "2026-04-29T02:11:51.601048", "query": "I'm enrolled in the NexCare Plus plan and I have $800 left in my Healthcare FSA at year end. How much of that can I roll over into next year, and where did I get that number?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 8}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 7}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "13.2 Offboarding Checklist", "chunk_index": 100}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "7.1 Health, Dental & Vision Insurance", "chunk_index": 53}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "7.2 Qualifying Life Events (QLE)", "chunk_index": 40}], "final_answer": "You have $800 left in your Healthcare FSA at year-end. According to the policy for the NexCare Plus plan, you can roll over a maximum of $660 into the next year. This means you will forfeit the remaining $140. \n\nTo summarize, you should expect to see $660 rolled over into your Healthcare FSA for the next plan year, while the excess amount of $140 will not be available for use.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees\n2. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 13.2 Offboarding Checklist\n3. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 7.1 Health, Dental & Vision Insurance\n4. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 7.2 Qualifying Life Events (QLE)", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "cba02884-703c-4f31-89cb-196b2d7c67f4", "session_id": "666fce05-a3e1-4119-9fa5-36c77e5b3820", "user_id": "d976e6a6-dcee-4072-859d-0c36b07e89c8", "timestamp": "2026-04-29T02:12:30.734861", "query": "I work remotely as a project manager. My internet bill is $85/month. Can I get reimbursed for it?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement", "section_header": "NEXARION SOLUTIONS, INC.", "chunk_index": 11}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Remote Work Technology Supplement", "section_header": "NEXARION SOLUTIONS, INC.", "chunk_index": 10}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "NEXARION SOLUTIONS, INC.", "chunk_index": 40}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "NEXARION SOLUTIONS, INC.", "chunk_index": 41}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "NEXARION SOLUTIONS, INC.", "chunk_index": 2}], "final_answer": "As a project manager, you are not eligible for reimbursement of your internet bill. The policy states that only employees in roles formally designated as Fully Remote Exempt (FRE) can receive reimbursement for ongoing internet costs. Currently, project managers do not fall under this designation, which means you will need to cover the $85/month internet expense yourself.", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "da1b2e66-6ed2-40b8-b664-c0542f4c7729", "session_id": "666fce05-a3e1-4119-9fa5-36c77e5b3820", "user_id": "d976e6a6-dcee-4072-859d-0c36b07e89c8", "timestamp": "2026-04-29T02:12:59.368292", "query": "I'm a California-based employee and I've accumulated 28 days of PTO. My annual accrual is 18 days (I'm in my 4th year). My manager told me anything over 26 days gets forfeited on January 1. Is that right?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "1.1 PTO Accrual & Carryover - California Override", "chunk_index": 5}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "NEXARION SOLUTIONS, INC.", "chunk_index": 61}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "Section 14: Acknowledgment of Receipt", "chunk_index": 103}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "NEXARION SOLUTIONS, INC.", "chunk_index": 60}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "1.1 PTO Accrual & Carryover - California Override", "chunk_index": 6}], "final_answer": "You have accumulated 28 days of PTO, and according to California law, you cannot forfeit any of your earned PTO. The policy states that California employees may accumulate PTO without a carryover cap, and any unused PTO cannot be forfeited. \n\nHowever, Nexarion may impose an accrual cap, which is 1.5 times your annual accrual rate. Since your annual accrual is 18 days, your accrual cap would be 27 days (1.5 x 18 days). This means that once you reach 27 days, further accrual will pause until your balance drops below this cap. \n\nIn your case, since you have 28 days, you will not lose any PTO, but you will not accrue any additional days until your balance falls below 27 days. To avoid losing any PTO, you may want to consider using some of your accrued days.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 1.1 PTO Accrual & Carryover - California Override\n2. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 Section 14: Acknowledgment of Receipt", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": false}
{"entry_id": "16f5527f-db3c-4f99-bfc5-fe83ad5560b6", "session_id": "666fce05-a3e1-4119-9fa5-36c77e5b3820", "user_id": "d976e6a6-dcee-4072-859d-0c36b07e89c8", "timestamp": "2026-04-29T02:13:48.035806", "query": "I just turned 62. What is the maximum I can contribute to my 401(k) this year, including catch-up contributions?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "Section 3: 401(k) Retirement Plan - Detailed Guide", "chunk_index": 13}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "SECURE 2.0)", "chunk_index": 14}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees", "chunk_index": 5}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 7}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "3.3 Loan and Hardship Withdrawal Provisions", "chunk_index": 19}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "13.3 COBRA Continuation Coverage", "chunk_index": 101}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "Section 10: Disciplinary Procedures", "chunk_index": 85}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "12.3 Confidentiality & Non-Disclosure", "chunk_index": 96}], "final_answer": "Since you just turned 62, you can contribute a maximum of $34,750 to your 401(k) for this year. This total includes the standard employee elective deferral limit of $23,500 and the enhanced catch-up contribution of $11,250 available to individuals aged 60 to 63. \n\nTo maximize your contributions, ensure that you adjust your contribution settings with your plan administrator, Fidelity Investments, if you haven't done so already. This will allow you to take full advantage of the catch-up contributions available to you this year.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 Section 3: 401(k) Retirement Plan - Detailed Guide\n2. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 SECURE 2.0)\n3. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees\n4. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees\n5. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 3.3 Loan and Hardship Withdrawal Provisions\n6. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 13.3 COBRA Continuation Coverage\n7. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 Section 10: Disciplinary Procedures", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "af76b414-09ac-48a2-aebf-5d14d5d20890", "session_id": "7f53169e-dd22-49ec-a96a-3a3dda31f5a0", "user_id": "d976e6a6-dcee-4072-859d-0c36b07e89c8", "timestamp": "2026-04-29T02:14:23.546221", "query": "I'm a New York-based employee and I've been out sick for 2 days. My manager is asking me to provide a doctor's note to use my PTO for those days. Do I have to provide one?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "3.1 Pre-Employment Requirements", "chunk_index": 18}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "4.2 Voluntary Supplemental Life Insurance", "chunk_index": 21}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "2.1 New York Paid Sick Leave", "chunk_index": 16}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "2.1 New York Paid Sick Leave", "chunk_index": 17}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.5 Dependent Care FSA", "chunk_index": 9}], "final_answer": "You are not required to provide a doctor's note to use your PTO for the 2 days you were out sick. According to the policy, employers in New York cannot require documentation for sick leave of fewer than 3 consecutive days. Therefore, you should be able to use your PTO without any additional documentation. If your manager insists on a doctor's note, you can refer them to this policy.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 3.1 Pre-Employment Requirements\n2. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 4.2 Voluntary Supplemental Life Insurance\n3. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 2.1 New York Paid Sick Leave\n4. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.5 Dependent Care FSA", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": false}
